rawn. The +327%/+442% prompt and +20%/+24% decode figures elsewhere in this row remain g64 numbers and must not be read as g128 ones. The x86 Q2_0 `vec_dot` fast path added alongside it is **not** covered by this toggle — see the default cell. | Reachable for a **g64** Q1_0/Q2_0 model and, since 2026-07-29 (lane-110F), for a **g128** `Q2_0_G128` model, and on a Vulkan-enabled build only with `--no-host`. **ADJUDICATED 2026-07-24 (bit-divergence round).** Bit-identity is **not achievable and was never the right bar** — proven against upstream's own repack types on this same binary (cost cell). The slot is now **correct and measured**. **DEFAULT OFF is IMPLEMENTED, not merely recommended** (flipped 2026-07-24, verified on a rebuilt binary — see the cost cell). The reason is unchanged: on a Vulkan-enabled build repacked weights lose GPU-offload eligibility and prompt processing regresses ~77–88%; on a CPU-only path the same slot is a **+327% to +442% prompt and +20% to +24% decode** win, so it stays compiled in and one `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=1` away. Set it to `1` for a CPU-only deployment; leave it unset everywhere else. The lane merges, not the executor. | **NaN FIXED (2026-07-24). Bit-divergence ADJUDICATED as INHERENT to the repack design, not a residual bug. Performance MEASURED (2026-07-24).**<br><br>**Root cause (one defect class, four sites).** PrismML's tree has `QK2_0 = 128`, so `QK2_0/QK8_0 = 4` and their kernels hardcode the activation-block stride as the literal `4`. This fork is canonical g64 (`QK2_0 = 64`, `ggml/src/ggml-common.h:187`), where the ratio is **2**. Every ported site that hardcoded `4` advanced the `block_q8_0` activation pointer twice as fast as its loop consumed, running past the packed activation buffer. **This is a downstream g64 integration defect, not a defect in PrismML's tree** — at g128 every one of these literals is correct.<br><br>**Fix A — the GEMM (4 lines, 2 files).** `ggml_gemm_q2_0_4x8_q8_0` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp:6664,6681`) and `ggml_gemm_q2_0_4x8_q8_0_generic` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp:2767,2786`): `(4 * y * nb)` → `(y * nb * (QK2_0 / QK8_0))` and `a_ptr + 4 * l + k` → `a_ptr + l * (QK2_0 / QK8_0) + k`, matching the form `ggml_gemv_q2_0_4x8_q8_0` already used correctly at `:6614`. Out-of-bounds `a_blk->d[m]` had been decoding as FP16 NaN and poisoning the FMA accumulator. The **Q1_0 arms were deliberately left alone**: `QK1_0 = 128`, so their hardcoded `4` is correct for this fork's current Q1 format — a portability hazard, not a present defect.<br><br>**Fix B — the control arm was itself broken (2 lines, separate commit).** The ported x86 `ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c`, added by `c7645a0df`) carried the same g128 literals in **both** its VNNI branch and its scalar `#else`: `for (int k = 0; k < 4; k++)` over `&y[i * 4 + k]`, plus `&x[i].qs[k * 8]` reading at offsets 16 and 24 of a **16-byte** `block_q2_0.qs`. Since it is compile-time-selected, `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=0` could not disable it. **Consequence: every ON/OFF comparison recorded in this slot before 2026-07-24 compared one broken kernel against a differently broken kernel, and none of them adjudicated anything.** The generic `ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0_generic` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/quants.c:203-204`) was already correct (`k < 2`, `y[i * 2 + k]`); the x86 arm now matches it via `QK2_0 / QK8_0`. This also retires the prior registry claim that this fast path was “bit-exact with the scalar loop it replaces” — **falsified**.<br><br>**Engagement proven, both arms, both models** (llama-server per F-085, `-ngl 0 -c 1024 -t 8 --no-host`, temp 0, top_k 1, seed 42, `cache_prompt` false, fresh server per arm, env flip only, same binary). ON: `load_tensors: CPU_REPACK model buffer size = 4.68 MiB` (Q8_0 base + 4× `ffn_down`) and `95.98 MiB` (all-Q2_0). OFF: **no `CPU_REPACK` line at all**. **Correction:** the prior row claimed `CPU_Mapped` “grows by the same amount” when repack is off. It does **not** — `CPU_Mapped` was `625.75 MiB` in *both* arms; the repack buffer is an additional allocation and the mmap accounting is unchanged. (The prior run's own numbers, 322.28 + 95.98 ON vs 323.45 OFF, already contradicted it.)<br><br>**Result, `qwen2.5-0.5b-light-q8_0-4xffndownQ2_0-g64.gguf`, 11-token prefill (GEMM path):** the NaN is **gone**. ON is finite, coherent and deterministic 3/3 (`md5 bf102b7715220e6f6df074626ede9a0e`), and after Fix B the OFF arm produces the **token-identical** continuation — same md5, all 32 tokens, deterministic 3/3 in both arms. Before Fix B the arms disagreed completely (ON coherent, OFF `“ering!!!!…”`). Independent check: the unquantized `qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-fp16.gguf` on the identical prompt continues `“ the dog jumps over the lazy cat. What is the next…”` (6/6 identical), which the repacked arm tracks closely.<br><br>**Bit-identity: NOT achieved, and ADJUDICATED as INHERENT (2026-07-24).** The ON/OFF logprob divergence is real (both arms internally deterministic, 3/3 rolls each) but it is **a property of llama.cpp's repack design, not of this port**. Proven with an upstream-blessed control: four additional models were quantised from the *same* `qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-fp16.gguf` source with the *same* Q8_0 base and the *same* four tensors (`blk.0-3.ffn_down`, `4864x896`) carrying an **upstream** repack type instead of Q2_0, then run through the identical protocol on the identical binary. `--no-repack` was used as a uniform OFF for every arm and is byte-for-byte equivalent to `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=0` on the Q2_0 model (identical logprob fingerprint `3dea625c`, 3/3 rolls). Results, max absolute delta-logprob over 32 tokens: **ours Q2_0 4x8 = `0.061002`** (mean `0.0123761`, token-identical); **upstream Q2_K 8x8 = `0.140226`** (mean `0.0263535`, token-identical); **upstream Q4_K 8x8 = `1.39052`** (mean `0.328262`, and it **changes the generated text**). Upstream's own blessed repack types are therefore *less* faithful to their scalar paths than this port is to its own. Mechanism class is acknowledged upstream in-tree: `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp:210` comments that the repack activation quantiser is divided by `127.f` "to mirror results in quantize_row_q8_0" — a *mirror*, not an identity. **The prior demand for bit-identity was the wrong acceptance bar and is withdrawn.**<br><br>**Upstream 8x8 repack SEGFAULTS on this box — pre-existing, NOT this branch.** Three of the five upstream repack types could not be run at all: Q4_0 (`q4_0_8x8`), IQ4_NL (`iq4_nl_8x8`) and MXFP4 (`mxfp4_8x8`) all abort with `0xC0000005` ACCESS_VIOLATION once `--no-host` makes `CPU_REPACK` reachable, after the buffer is allocated (`CPU_REPACK model buffer size = 9.35 / 9.35 / 8.83 MiB`). gdb frame 0 is `ggml_gemv_q4_0_8x8_q8_0`, frame 1 `ggml::cpu::repack::tensor_traits<block_q4_0, 8ll, 8ll, (ggml_type)8>::compute_forward`, reached from `llama_decode` on a libgomp worker. **Attribution settled: stock upstream `llama-upstream-b10068` (`src/llama-upstream-b10068/build-vulkan/bin/llama-server.exe`) reproduces the identical crash on the identical model** — and this branch is strictly additive over its own base commit `f7c4d9d2c` (`git diff --numstat f7c4d9d2c..e32bf4149`: zero deletions in `repack.cpp`, `arch/x86/repack.cpp` and `arch/x86/quants.c`; the only deletion across the branch's nine commits is one `arch-fallback.h` alias). **Topology correction — RESOLVED 2026-07-24 (rebase round).** `f7c4d9d2c` is *not* master; it is the tag `pre-linearize-2026-07-24`, a merge commit on a parallel lineage. Master was then LINEARIZED to **`279f59f11`** (linear series, no fork merge commits); `67c83a6ec` is now an intermediate commit on that line, not the tip. The two lines diverged at `e70805586`. **The rebase is DONE:** `git rebase --onto master pre-linearize-2026-07-24 topic/vnni-repack` replayed all twelve commits with **zero conflicts**, and the resulting delta is byte-identical to the pre-rebase delta (same 